Joplin 3.7.21: license, source and configuration

The official Linux x86_64 package is downloaded unchanged from:
https://github.com/laurent22/joplin/releases/download/v3.7.21/Joplin-3.7.21.deb
SOURCE.json pins its SHA-256 digest. solve.sh unpacks its data archive without
running Debian maintainer scripts. The two bundled default plugins are omitted:
io.github.jackgruber.backup and io.github.personalizedrefrigerator.js-draw.
The executable, app.asar and runtime libraries are unchanged.

Joplin is licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later, except where a component has its own
license. LICENSE contains the full GNU AGPL version 3. LICENSES/joplin.txt
preserves the upstream license-scope, trademark, logo and icon notices. Joplin
is a trademark of JOPLIN SAS. Logos and icons remain subject to the upstream
notice and are used only within the distributed product package.

Corresponding source is version v3.7.21, commit
e41516e669efb693b009bedb21f3eb1fcbea4fc9 of https://github.com/laurent22/joplin:
https://codeload.github.com/laurent22/joplin/tar.gz/refs/tags/v3.7.21
The source archive is downloaded and verified alongside the release package.
SOURCE.json records its digest. The unmodified source and its component notices
remain available in that archive.

LICENSES/electron.txt, LICENSES/chromium.txt, LICENSES/7zip.txt and
LICENSES/tesseract-js-core.txt contain the notices distributed with those
components. chromium.txt is the complete text content of the package's
LICENSES.chromium.html, with only HTML presentation removed. The original HTML
and the Node module license files remain in the package and extracted runtime.

The environment also builds unmodified libfaketime 0.9.13, licensed under GPL-2.0.
Its complete license is LICENSES/libfaketime.txt and its corresponding source is
retained at environment/libfaketime-0.9.13.tar.gz. It can be obtained from:
https://codeload.github.com/wolfcw/libfaketime/tar.gz/refs/tags/v0.9.13
The component version and digest are recorded in SOURCE.json.

Local start.sh and launch.py configure DATA_DIR/profile, enable the Data API
using PORT and PBP_API_TOKEN, disable first-run update checks and OCR, and run
with --no-sandbox, --force-renderer-accessibility, --no-welcome and --profile.
The foreground supervisor forwards signals and retries one immediate clean
startup exit before any product window appears. These launchers are separate
from upstream code. This task is not affiliated with or endorsed by JOPLIN SAS.

The local confinement.py applies Landlock before product execution, restricting
file access and external programs while retaining required private data, exchange
folders and application workers. It refuses unconfined startup.

The GUI starts in the document outbox so file dialogs open a readable exchange
directory while the installation root remains non-enumerable.
